From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wineps: makers' PostScript render plug-ins (IPrintOemPS/IPrintOemPS2)

Makers' PostScript drivers add a render plug-in to the system's
PostScript core for job accounting, user codes, finishing and PJL
(Ricoh, Xerox, Kyocera, Konica Minolta, Canon...). The package's .ini
names it ([OEMFiles] OEMDriverFile1); we ignored it. Now, from the
documented plug-in interfaces:

- The core creates each plug-in as a COM object, hands it its helper
  (IPrintOemDriverPS: DrvGetDriverSetting for the chosen PPD options,
  DrvWriteSpoolBuf), sets up its devmode part (DevMode size/defaults) and
  enables it (EnablePDEV with the DEVOBJ, whose pDrvProcs table older
  plug-ins write through).
- IPrintCorePS2 answers what plug-ins ask of the PPD: the chosen options
  (GetOptions), its features and options (EnumFeatures, EnumOptions,
  including the ones wineps handles itself: PageSize, InputSlot,
  Duplex), and global, feature and option attributes.
- The plug-in's Command is called at the job's injection points (the
  stream's start before the JCL, %!PS-Adobe, the prolog, the setup, each
  page's setup, the page's end, the trailer, %%EOF, the stream's end).
- A plug-in whose IPrintOemPS2::WritePrinter answers a call without data
  sees the whole job on its way out and writes it to the printer itself.

Ricoh's PostScript driver now prints with its plug-in's job code.

Test: test/psplugin-gate.sh with test/psplugin-plugin.c, our own plug-in
and PPD (mutants SG_MUTANT_PSPLUGIN, PSINJECT, PSWRITE, COREPS2,
PSPROCS, BUILTINFEATURES).
---
--- a/dlls/wineps.drv/escape.c
+++ b/dlls/wineps.drv/escape.c
@@ -44,7 +44,11 @@
 
     if (ctx->job.data_cnt)
     {
-        if (!WritePrinter(ctx->job.hprinter, ctx->job.data, ctx->job.data_cnt, &written) ||
+        if (ps_plugins_write( ctx, ctx->job.data, ctx->job.data_cnt, &written ))
+        {
+            if (written != ctx->job.data_cnt) return FALSE;
+        }
+        else if (!WritePrinter(ctx->job.hprinter, ctx->job.data, ctx->job.data_cnt, &written) ||
                 written != ctx->job.data_cnt)
             return FALSE;
     }
@@ -64,7 +68,11 @@
 
     if (ctx->job.data_cnt + num > ARRAY_SIZE(ctx->job.data))
     {
-        if (!WritePrinter(ctx->job.hprinter, (LPBYTE) data, num, &written) ||
+        if (ps_plugins_write( ctx, data, num, &written ))
+        {
+            if (written != num) return SP_OUTOFDISK;
+        }
+        else if (!WritePrinter(ctx->job.hprinter, (LPBYTE) data, num, &written) ||
                 written != num)
             return SP_OUTOFDISK;
     }
